    "content": "---\n\n> **PAGE:** `/industries/food-delivery/`  \n> **SOURCE FILE:** `wave1-generated/industries/food-delivery.md`\n\n\n\n\n# Software Development for Food Delivery\n\n**Delivery economics are routing plus batching plus refund discipline — software decides the margin.** Clickmasters builds custom software for US food delivery organizations — the operational systems, portals, and integrations that fit how the work actually happens, with [AI capabilities](/services/ai-application-development/) applied where they measurably pay.\n\n[Trust bar: [PLACEHOLDER — industry proof points]]\n\n## What We Build for Food Delivery\n\n- **Dispatch and courier apps with proof-of-delivery**\n- **Marketplace or first-party ordering platforms**\n- **Refund and exception workflows that stop leakage**\n- **[AI where it pays](/services/ai-application-development/)** — document intelligence, workflow agents with approval gates, and assistants grounded in your data — measured, never demo-ware\n\n## The Industry Reality We Build Around\n\nEvery industry has its non-negotiables — the compliance posture, the operational rhythm, the integration estate — and discovery here starts by documenting yours from the people who live them. Software that ignores industry texture gets routed around; software that encodes it becomes how the work is done. [PLACEHOLDER — 2–3 sentences of original industry insight from your delivery experience; required before indexing.]\n\n## Custom vs Off-the-Shelf in Food Delivery\n\nThe honest routing that runs our whole practice: where industry-standard tools genuinely fit, use them and keep your money — we'll say so in the first call. The build case appears where your workflows diverge from the template, where per-seat pricing punishes your team structure, or where the tools you're paying for still leave the core work in spreadsheets. The [build-vs-buy math](/frameworks/build-vs-buy/) with your numbers is the scoping call's first deliverable.\n\n## Recent Food Delivery Work\n\n> **[PLACEHOLDER — 1–2 verifiable industry case studies. Required before indexing.]**\n\n## FAQ\n\n**Do you have food delivery experience?**\n[PLACEHOLDER — answer honestly with real experience, adjacent-industry transfer, or the domain-immersion process. Never fabricate credentials.]\n\n**What does industry software cost?**\nFocused systems typically start at [PLACEHOLDER]; integration depth and compliance scope drive the range. Fixed-milestone quotes always — see the [cost guides](/resources/software-cost-guides/).\n\n**Can you integrate with our industry systems?**\nIntegration is usually the center of industry work — your existing platforms, data flows, and the reconciliation discipline that keeps systems agreeing.\n\n**How do you handle our compliance requirements?**\nCompliance is architecture, not paperwork after the fact — your regulatory posture becomes build requirements with audit trails to match. Your counsel owns the legal positions; we make them executable.\n\n**Where does AI actually help in our industry?**\nWhere volume meets pattern: document intake, status communication, exception triage — [measured deployments](/solutions/ai-agents/) with approval gates, never autonomy on day one.\n\n---\n\n### Book an Industry Consultation\nBring your workflow and your current stack — leave with an honest assessment and a scoped path.\n[Form] [Calendar embed]",
