    "url": "/industries/real-estate/",
    "meta": {
      "title": "Real Estate Software Development Company | Clickmasters",
      "description": "Real estate software development — property management platforms, MLS/IDX integration, tenant portals, proptech products & real estate CRMs built to close."
    },
    "content": "---\n\n> **PAGE:** `/industries/real-estate/`  \n> **SOURCE FILE:** `wave0-batch5/ind04-real-estate.md`\n\n\n# INDUSTRY 04 — Real Estate\n\n\n\n# Real Estate Software Development Company\n\n**Real estate software development spans the systems that run property businesses — management platforms, tenant and owner portals, real-estate CRMs, listing and MLS/IDX integrations — and the proptech products trying to reinvent them.** Clickmasters builds both for US brokerages, property managers, investors, and proptech founders: software shaped around the industry's actual units of work — the listing, the lease, the transaction, the unit turn — rather than generic CRM abstractions with \"property\" fields bolted on.\n\nThe industry-specific insight that shapes everything we build here: **real estate runs on transactions with long lifecycles and many parties** — a lease touches applicant, guarantor, agent, manager, owner, and maintenance; a sale touches buyer, seller, two agents, lender, title, and inspectors. Software that models these as simple records produces the email-and-spreadsheet shadow system every brokerage secretly runs. Software that models the *workflow* — states, parties, documents, deadlines, and money — replaces it. [Book a consultation](#consult) and bring your messiest transaction; that's the one we design around.\n\n[Trust bar: real estate clients · doors/units under management on our systems (if real) · reviews]\n\n## What We Build\n\n| System | Who it serves | Built around |\n|---|---|---|\n| **[Property management platforms](/solutions/property-management-software/)** | PMs, landlords, HOAs | Leases, rent collection (ACH/card), maintenance workflows, owner statements & distributions |\n| **Tenant & owner [portals](/solutions/customer-portal/)** | Residents, investors | Payments, requests, documents, announcements — the call-deflection layer |\n| **Real estate [CRMs](/solutions/crm-development/)** | Brokerages, teams | Lead routing, drip follow-up, transaction pipelines, commission math (the part vendors get wrong) |\n| **Listing platforms & MLS/IDX integration** | Brokerages, portals | RESO Web API feeds, listing sync, search UX that respects MLS display rules |\n| **[Marketplace & investment platforms](/solutions/marketplace-development/)** | Proptech founders | Two-sided mechanics, escrow-adjacent flows, KYC where investment scope requires ([fintech crossover →](/industries/fintech/)) |\n| **Maintenance & [field ops](/solutions/field-service-management/)** | PM ops teams, vendors | Work orders, vendor dispatch, photo documentation, mobile-first for the tech in the crawlspace |\n| **Short-term & [booking systems](/solutions/booking-system/)** | STR operators | Calendars, channel sync (Airbnb/Vrbo-class), dynamic pricing hooks, turnover ops |\n| **Underwriting & analytics tools** | Investors, acquisitions teams | Deal models, comps ingestion, portfolio dashboards — [BI done properly →](/solutions/analytics-dashboards/) |\n| **[Real estate AI](/services/ai-application-development/)** | All of the above | Lead-response agents, document intelligence (leases/offers into structured data), listing-content drafting with human review, maintenance-triage bots |\n\n## The Integration Landscape\n\nReal estate builds live inside an ecosystem, and we speak its dialects: **MLS via RESO Web API** (and the per-MLS quirks the standard politely ignores) · IDX display-compliance rules · payment rails for rent and deposits ([Stripe](/platforms/stripe/)/ACH with the state-by-state deposit-handling awareness) · accounting (QuickBooks/property-specific GLs, trust-account separation) · e-signature (DocuSign-class) in transaction flows · background/credit screening providers in leasing · and Zillow/portal lead feeds into CRM routing. Every integration ships with the [exception-queue discipline](/services/api-development/) that keeps bad data from silently corrupting a transaction file.\n\n## Compliance Notes Buyers Ask About\n\nFair-housing-aware design (advertising surfaces, screening workflows, and AI features reviewed so automation can't encode discrimination — this is a design review we run deliberately) · trust/escrow account separation in anything touching deposits or owner funds · state-specific security-deposit and notice rules modeled as configuration, not hardcoded assumptions · TCPA-aware texting workflows in CRM follow-up. The honest boundary: your broker counsel owns the legal theory; we make the software match it and keep the audit trail.\n\n## Recent Real Estate Work\n\n> **[PLACEHOLDER — 2–3 case studies: e.g., \"PM platform for X-thousand doors: rent collection automated, owner statements from 3 days to 1 hour\"; \"brokerage CRM: lead response time from A to B minutes\" — verifiable only]**\n\n## Cost Context\n\nPortals and CRMs: **$50K–$150K**. Property management platforms: **$120K–$350K+** (payments, accounting, and state-rule configurability are the drivers). Listing/marketplace products: **$80K–$300K** with MLS integration itemized per feed. [Cost guides →](/resources/software-cost-guides/)\n\n## FAQ\n\n**Can you integrate with our MLS?**\nYes — via RESO Web API where offered (most US MLSs now), with the per-board approval process and display-rule compliance handled as part of scope. Multi-MLS brokerages get a normalization layer so your product sees one schema, not thirty.\n\n**Buy Yardi/AppFolio/Buildium — or build?**\nBuy when your operation fits their model and the per-unit fees pencil out; build when your workflow *is* your edge (niche asset classes, unusual fee structures, owner-experience differentiation) or when platform fees at your door count exceed ownership cost. We'll run the [build-vs-buy math](/frameworks/build-vs-buy/) with your numbers — and hybrid (keep their accounting, build your ops layer) is often the honest winner.\n\n**Can you handle rent payments and owner distributions?**\nYes — ACH/card collection, late-fee logic per state config, trust-account-separated flows, and owner statements with distributions — engineered with the [ledger discipline](/industries/fintech/) money deserves, because a PM platform is quietly a fintech product.\n\n**Where does AI actually pay in real estate now?**\nSpeed-to-lead agents (responding to portal leads in seconds, booking showings, with human handoff), lease and offer document extraction, maintenance-request triage, and listing-content drafting with agent review. All with [approval gates](/services/ai-agent-development/) — and fair-housing review on anything tenant-facing.\n\n**How long does a build take?**\nPortals and CRMs: 3–5 months. Management platforms: 6–10 months, shipped module-by-module — rent collection first is the usual ROI-ordering.\n\n**We're a proptech startup, not an operator. Same team?**\nSame team, different track: [MVP discipline](/services/mvp-development/), [SaaS architecture](/services/saas-development/), and the industry-integration fluency above — which is precisely the combination proptech founders struggle to hire.\n\n---\n\n### [#consult] Book a Real Estate Software Consultation\nBring the messiest transaction and the tool stack — leave with a workflow-shaped architecture sketch and a phased quote.\n[Form] [Calendar embed]",
